  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraqi workers&#x2019; organizations have an important role in contributing to labour policy discussions, but their capacity to develop structured, evidence-based policy proposals and engage effectively in social dialogue mechanisms remains limited. This intervention will support participating Iraqi trade unions to strengthen their policy development and advocacy capacities and to prepare concrete trade union proposals on priority labour issues, including occupational safety and health, wages and labour rights. The activity will also support the presentation and discussion of these proposals in relevant national social dialogue and tripartite mechanisms, in line with the Right to Organise and Collective Bargaining Convention, 1949 (No. 98). It will contribute to strengthening workers&#x2019; organizations&#x2019; ability to influence policymaking and ensure that workers&#x2019; priorities are reflected in labour policy discussions.</narrative>
  </description>
